Z||000000||ElricSI||07-04-2001||12:03 PM||||Time and time again I see or hear about a Fiero that might be interesting to buy, but whoever is selling it wants too much or ** WAY ** too much for the car.  Anyway let me see if this link works:<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592851196" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592851196</A> <P>Ooh good, it did.  Anyway that is a real nice car but the price seems out of wack to what he is really going to get for it, maybe if it had some great mods.  I have been guily of asking a little too much for mine, but then I don't really want to part with it.<P>P.S. Does anyone else notice that lots of people seem to be wanting to get rid of 85 or 86 Fieros right now?  Seems to be kind of a glut.  87 and 88 sales seem normal.  Most 84's must be dead by now.<P>------------------<BR>Proud Owner of 85 GT<p>[This message has been edited by ElricSI (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tina||07-04-2001||12:19 PM||||Hear you there.<BR>Reminds me of the the guy I ran into with his<BR>86 GT<BR>Granted the car was in very good shape,well maintained, no rips or tears, and below 100thousand miles.<BR>But come on,valued at $15.000 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Tina||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||07-04-2001||01:27 PM||||Let's assume for a moment that the blue '87 is in perfect condition, has original paint in perfect condition, great maintenance (records would help here), fully loaded, etc.  It only has 55k miles on it (I didn't look much farther), too.  My wifes' '98 Cavalier is worth around 7 large and it has about the same miles, but absolutely no options whatsoever with 2 exceptions.  It has A/C (damn cold, I might add) and an aftermarket CD player (generic head unit).  I probably wouldn't pay 7 grand for the Fiero, but it's probably worth that much if you compare it to anything else out there.<P>Just my 2/100th of a dollar.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000003||ElricSI||07-04-2001||01:51 PM||||Let me merely say I love that car.  I would pay extra cause it's blue.  I just don't think he's gonna get 7000 for it unless someone HAS to have a blue one and has money to burn.  (If I had that much money to burn, I might buy it.)<P>------------------<BR>Proud Owner of 85 GT||||reg||6
Z||000004||mblackwell||07-04-2001||02:19 PM||||Deep down on the subconcious level, they don't really want to get rid of thier Fieros.  Who would?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000005||Predator||07-04-2001||03:22 PM||||It is probably a guy who's wife said he had to sell his Fiero, and he said ok. I'll ask so much no one will buy it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. That way the wife is happy and he gets to keep his car, and if anybody gives him the $7,000 then he can buy two Fiero's to take it's place..<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Predator (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||rodmcneill||07-04-2001||03:27 PM||||He was asking $8500.00 in the local paper for this car. I guess he had no responses.||||reg||1
Z||000007||dlancer407||07-04-2001||07:16 PM||||Hi All; I have been a Fiero owner for all of a month now. One thing I have noticed is that you can pick up a Fiero for almost any price. Thats the the great thing about these cars. If you have $500 or $ 10,000.00 you can find a car that falls into your budget.I bought my 85 GT off of Ebay for $1,400.00. I had a little more money to spend but now I can use it for some mods. With a lot of other collector cars you need tons of money just to get in the game.||||reg||7
Z||000008||maryjane||07-04-2001||09:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ElricSI:<BR><B>Time and time again I see or hear about a Fiero that might be interesting to buy, but whoever is selling it wants too much or ** WAY ** too much for the car.  Anyway let me see if this link works:<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592851196" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592851196</A> <P>Ooh good, it did.  Anyway that is a real nice car but the price seems out of wack to what he is really going to get for it, maybe if it had some great mods.  I have been guily of asking a little too much for mine, but then I don't really want to part with it.<P>P.S. Does anyone else notice that lots of people seem to be wanting to get rid of 85 or 86 Fieros right now?  Seems to be kind of a glut.  87 and 88 sales seem normal.  Most 84's must be dead by now.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My '84 isn't dead (sick, but not dead). But you're right, even the local ones are high. Last one I saw here was an'85-a/c broke, wiper motor removed and in the baggage comp,100k + miles. Wanted $1500. Paint only fair, interior -a lot of wear. It was 3 mos ago, still sittin there. <P>------------------<BR>84 SE 2.5<BR>not slow not fast-just halfast||||reg||1
